# HP48gII full stock launch: stock Kermit -> ARMToolbox48 -> hpclang HPC1.
2000 tap f6
4000 tap f6
# Factory default is ALG; use RPN for the stack-based library install.
5000 tap mode
5500 tap neg
6000 tap f6
7000 capture home-rpn
# Configure wire I/O to Serial.
8000 tap files
9500 tap down
10000 tap enter
11500 tap down
12000 tap down
12500 tap down
13000 tap down
14000 tap enter
16000 tap up
17000 tap f2
18000 tap down
18500 tap enter
20000 tap enter
# Start stock Kermit server.
22000 tap files
23500 tap down
24500 tap enter
26000 tap down
27000 tap down
28000 tap down
29000 tap down
30000 tap down
31500 tap enter
33500 capture server-serial
# The host starts Kermit at t=35s. Do not guess how long the transfer takes:
# pause all following sequence actions until the host reports successful Kermit
# completion through HPCLANG_E2E_HOST_GATE_FILE. Times below are relative to
# that release, not to emulator start.
35000 host-gate
1000 capture after-transfer
# Install ARMToolbox48 Library 275 into Port 0. With both variables present,
# HPCLANG is F1 and L275 is F2 in the HOME VAR menu.
2000 tap var
3000 capture vars-before-install
4000 tap f2
5000 capture l275-stack
6000 tap zero
7000 tap enter
8000 capture port-zero-stack
9000 tap sto
11000 capture stored
13000 chord on f3
19000 capture after-warmstart
# L275 moved to Port 0; HPCLANG remains the first HOME variable.
20000 tap var
21000 capture vars-after-install
22000 tap f1
24000 capture hpclang-stack
# Library 275 is the first LIB entry; ARMTo exposes PrRUN on F1.
26000 chord rshift two
27500 capture lib-menu
28500 tap f1
30500 capture armtoolbox
31000 monitor 60000
31500 tap f1
